<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Jefferson Smurfit acquires Argentine firms.</title>
<headline>Jefferson Smurfit acquires Argentine firms.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland's paper and linerboard manufacturer Jefferson Smurfit Group plc announced on Tuesday that it had acquired an 80 percent stake two paper companies in Argentina for around 17 million Irish pounds.</p>
<p>They are Celulosa de Coronel Suarez S.A. and Asindus S.A. Both the companies are located south of Buenos Aires, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Alan Smurfit, chairman of Smurfit Latin America, said the acquisitions would provide an opportunity towards the development of the packaging industry in Argentina.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom - 353-1-6613377</p>
</text>
